# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example environment file for Yocto Collection Companion.
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   A template listing every environment variable the app understands, with
#   safe default values. It is committed to git so anyone cloning the repo can
#   see which variables exist. It contains no secrets or machine-specific
#   values, which is why it is the ".example" (template) rather than the live
#   file.
#
# HOW TO USE IT
#   1. Copy it to a local `.env`:   cp .env.example .env
#   2. Edit `.env` with values for your machine (dev laptop, NAS, ...).
#   3. Run the app; `ycc.config.Settings` loads `.env` automatically.
#
#   `.env` is git-ignored, so your local (and any future secret) values are
#   never committed. Keep this template in sync whenever a new setting is
#   added to `ycc.config.Settings`.
#
# CONVENTIONS
#   - Every variable is prefixed with `YCC_`.
#   - Environment variables and `.env` entries override the defaults baked into
#     `ycc.config.Settings`; explicit values passed in code override both.
#   - Values shown below are the current defaults.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Human-readable application name, surfaced in the UI.
YCC_APP_NAME="Yocto Collection Companion"
